  "detail": null,
  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 4 members), per RBC-QM-02 (measurement period: calendar 2026).\n\n| Patient | Age at 12/31/2026 | Status | Reason / action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Open gap | No FIT, sDNA-FIT, sigmoidoscopy, CT colonography or colonoscopy found in coded data or notes. At first she looked excluded (frailty cond-00189 plus donepezil). But Dr. Lin's message today (comm-00301) says the frailty entry was put on her chart by mistake and is now marked entered in error. Without frailty, the frailty + advanced illness exclusion does not apply. No hospice/palliative care and no nursing home. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001, window 10/23–12/31/2026) and outreach message sent (comm-t0004). |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice care 6/16–8/21/2026 (eoc-00002, finished), confirmed by today's St. Brigid hospice discharge summary (doc-00402). She left hospice to join a clinical trial, but a finished hospice episode during the measurement period still excludes her. No order placed and no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 52 | Open gap | Her FIT (obs-01732) was first reported as collected 1/5/2026. Today the lab corrected the collection date to 12/31/2025; 1/5 was the date the lab received it. Stool tests count by collection date, so this one falls outside 2026. No other screening and no exclusions (her past cancers are oral, not colorectal). FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002) and outreach message sent (comm-t0005). |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap | Her 6/11/2024 sDNA-FIT (obs-01871) was withdrawn by Harbor Lab (specimen mislabeled, belongs to another patient; doc-00401) and is now entered in error. Her 2025 colonoscopy order sr-00003 was never done, and an order doesn't count as screening. No exclusions. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0003) and outreach message sent (comm-t0006). |\n\nNone of the three patients with an open gap had an active FIT order before. Each FIT window starts within 2026. The messages say the kit is on its way and explain how to collect, date and return it, with no claims about past screening.\n\nItems that arrived after I started (inbox-a0001 to a0004) were reviewed and closed with comments; the orders and messages above already reflect them. Other open inbox items are older and not about group members, so I left them alone. For Dr. Okafor's attention: pt-0024's old colonoscopy order sr-00003 (window ended 6/30/2025) is still active.",
  "resumed": false,
